Z||000006||V8Fiero||05-21-2001||11:07 PM||||Lisa: I think 84Bill was saying that you didnt appreciate the trophy that you got and what it stood for!<P>When I used to be into mini trucks I attended a many of shows and it didnt matter if I placed or not. I just really enjoyed the people and all the nice vehicles. I think that is the most important element.<P>The trophies and such are just an extra bonus.<P>Just an innocent bystanders perception.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||11:15 PM||||ALright people sorry. I know the trophy stood for something, and it does mean a lot to me, everyone saw me smiling like hell when I won it. <BR>So sorry for saying "stinking tophy" but it seems like you are just looking for an argument? I think its pretty obvious that I appreciate it and do a hell of a lot of work on my car to deserve it.<P>ANd the 5.99 pep boys seats? Thanks for the UNCALLED for insult??? That car was completely stock 3 mos ago, sorry its not at perfection. But dont you think saying that people shouldnt have voted for me is rude as hell?? Why don't you apologize for your wording on that.<P>Apparently you guys didn't understand my intentions on the last post. I don't need to explain myself, my motives, or my hardwork. ANyone who knows me knows that I work hard and I definitely deserved that trophy. But ARE TROPHIES EVERYTHING? No theyre not. If you didn't win a trophy at Carlisle, I'm pretty sure you still love your car. I think you all deserve one for putting in effort to get there and have nice clean cars.<P>I'm done defending myself, if you hate me, so be it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||05-21-2001||11:16 PM||||I have a feeling that Lisa's trophy comment was just inaccurately worded... I am *quite* sure that the Lisa I know wouldn't have meant it the way it sounded, nor the way people are taking it...<P>Especially after getting screwed into an incorrect (and non-judged) category at the pervious show, I'm sure that Lisa appreciates her win at Carlisle a lot more than her mischosen words indicate... let's give her the chance to state things a bit more clearly before we burn her at the stake, shall we? <P>EDIT - ah, she was typing at the same time I was... a bit defensively, but understandably so... <P>This doesn't have to turn from a misunderstanding into a flame war, does it...?<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
